Target: native AC090 68040 AmigaOS, canonical javascript.library v1
Toolchain: OpenAmigaGCC 16.2.0-open3
Native executable SHA256: ecaa1b9a8982f9006c8574130e886b505d5facb97f2157fa40464ab340a09115

Original source: OoliteProject/oolite pinned
src/Core/Scripting/OOJSEntity.m and Entity.h:
  collisionRadius, distanceTravelled, mass and spawnTime are read-only
  GLfloat-backed JavaScript properties.

Implementation: four more real OOJSEntity JSHostClass getters routed through
the game-owner Exec port, invoking native Objective-C selectors. An IEEE-754
binary32 float is carried bit-exactly as LONG in the existing RPC message,
then converted to a JavaScript Number. No ObjC selectors run on JSTask.

Native ACAgent output:
OOLITE_ENTITY_SCALARS_BEGIN
OOLITE_ENTITY_SCALARS code=0 write=1 result=42 rpc=8 done=1 closed=1 status=PASS
OOLITE_ENTITY_SCALARS_RC 0
OOLITE_ENTITY_SCALARS_END

The controlled ObjC fixture had collisionRadius=28.25,
distanceTravelled=1234.5, mass=90.5 and spawnTime=3.75.
JS evaluated all individual values and their sum 1357.0, result 42;
eight getter RPCs were serviced. A strict-mode attempt to assign
ship.mass=999 threw JSERR_EXCEPTION=1 as desired. The guest exited with
RC 0 and closed the game RPC port cleanly.

Limit: all source selectors match original pinned Entity.h but are backed by
the controlled ObjC ShipEntity fixture, not the full game/Universe.
